      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8e1f8bb3",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
      "label": "Mechanic mapped as 'tranny' in the joke",
      "description": "The text 'pick up a tranny' in the meme creates an analogical mapping where the visual entity 'mechanic' is implicitly mapped onto the textual entity 'tranny'. This mapping is based on the pun where 'tranny' refers to a manual transmission (a mechanical part) and is misapplied to refer to a transgender person. The mechanic, who is working on the car's engine (a mechanical part), is visually juxtaposed with the text to reinforce the crude, sexualized punchline. This mapping relies on the stereotype that mechanics are associated with mechanical 'parts', which is a form of objectification and reinforces harmful stereotypes about gender roles and professions.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dbea1061"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_eb64cff1",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the mechanic as the 'tranny'",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'mechanic' through the textual joke 'pick up a tranny'. The mechanic, who is visually working on the car's engine (a mechanical part), is implicitly mapped onto the slur 'tranny' (a derogatory term for a transgender person). This creates a crude, sexualized punchline that objectifies the mechanic and reinforces harmful stereotypes about gender roles and professions. The projection is implicit, relying on the pun and the visual juxtaposition, rather than explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you'.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dbea1061"
      },
